  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of Territorial Agendas for Youth in Peace Program (ATJP) for Preventing Recruitment and for the Promotion of Healthy Coexistence and Reconciliation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total Peace seeks to demobilize all actors persisting in the armed conflict and, at the same time, build a path that allows understanding and transforming the root causes of violence to overcome the cycles of conflict repetition that have destabilized society. To transform this reality, the 2022 - 2026 development plan &quot;Colombia Potencia Mundial de la vida&quot; has given special importance to youth in its proposals, thus implementing the National Youth for Peace Program aimed at youth living in poverty, vulnerability, and at risk of being involved in violent and criminal dynamics through educational, co-responsibility, and psychological, family, and community support components to create protective environments and reduce violence rates. Based on the above, this project aims to implement the Youth for Peace Program from the co-responsibility or social work component in collaboration between IOM and ARN through the formulation and implementation of Youth Territorial Agents for Peace as a comprehensive protection strategy for young people. In this regard, IOM&apos;s counterpart is represented by the transfer of best practices and lessons learned in community collaboration and technical assistance to strengthen the development and sustainability of productive initiatives that may arise from working with the youth in the Program.</narrative>
  </description>
